Debian source and runtime provenance
====================================

Upstream orig tarball
---------------------

Version 0.3.2 uses the deterministic upstream release asset, not a generated
GitHub snapshot:

  https://github.com/mitzracing/live-for-speed-linux/releases/download/v0.3.2/live-for-speed-linux-0.3.2.tar.gz
  SHA-256: a36b63ed70a652bca8987917e9bc26769a2f23930523292c764544d4e0faaa1a

Rename it to live-for-speed-linux_0.3.2.orig.tar.gz next to the unpacked source
before building the Debian source package. The archive contains the Expat
wrapper sources, CC0 AppStream metadata, and GPL-3.0-or-later public Arch
packager certificate. No proprietary or prebuilt runtime payload is present.
`debian/rules` builds and tests without network access.

The Debian draft uses revision 0.3.2-1. The published GitHub direct-download
package uses lower-sorting revision 0.3.2-0github1, so distinct package bytes do
not share a version and an official Debian package sorts newer.

Debian delta
------------

Upstream 0.3.2 contains the reviewed runtime hardening, signer certificate,
and regression fixtures previously carried in the Debian draft. This package
therefore has no quilt delta. The remaining Debian directory contains only
archive packaging, policy metadata, offline build and installed-package tests,
and the documented Wine ABI audit. Sponsor agreement on the external archived
Wine model and optional runtime-library boundary remains a pre-upload gate.

External runtime correspondence
-------------------------------

External payloads are downloaded only after an explicit user command, into a
per-user XDG directory. They are not Debian source or binary package content.
All three are pinned by URL, byte size, and SHA-256 in
share/lfs-linux/release.env and are verified before extraction or execution.

Wine:

* Downloaded binary: wine-11.15-1-x86_64.pkg.tar.zst
* Binary SHA-256: 5ee6a5522f81aba8441474c833552dd8f86bc9b9927c4efc9cb9251121124af4
* Detached signature SHA-256:
  c137f4dc493c7f8f00b47e42a014d19cdbbcac8b7daed41948b8f8148e3edc80
* Package signer: Peter Jung <ptr1337@archlinux.org>, fingerprint
  D2E95FEC015CF1F911AAAB0C3D4C5008BB5C8D29
* Signer identity: https://archlinux.org/people/package-maintainers/
* Shipped key SHA-256:
  c3186f2f7bdbe1cd02002dc84bce781580e4edc49fdc3ad848096af6768f3a89
* Key source: Arch keyring signed tag 20260727, commit
  cb5bbe4f36edae7a6bc7b3e373714dcde2cba7ae
* Arch packaging tag: 11.15-1 (signed annotated tag)
* Arch packaging commit: f70b597ed89e4e0beae53ace69b109eaff274648
* Recipe and auxiliary sources:
  https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/packaging/packages/wine/-/tree/11.15-1
* Upstream signed source tag: wine-11.15
  https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/tree/wine-11.15
* Upstream release tarball:
  https://dl.winehq.org/wine/source/11.x/wine-11.15.tar.xz
* Upstream tarball size: 46665288 bytes
* Upstream tarball SHA-256:
  5046f36dae210b198ea69792774d4401feed975d465eca6c251c9394400ec272
* License: LGPL-2.1-or-later

The Arch recipe applies no Wine source patch. It adds two integration files
and records their hashes in .SRCINFO. The exact build recipe, dependencies,
flags, valid Wine signing keys, and source-tree SHA-512 are retained at the
immutable Arch tag above. The wrapper verifies the detached package signature
against only the shipped signer certificate and exact fingerprint before
extracting Wine; this proves Arch packager authentication, not reproducible
binary-to-source correspondence. `debian/wine-runtime-audit.md` records a
complete ELF `DT_NEEDED` audit, including four optional module SONAMEs not
satisfied by current Debian unstable. Sponsor agreement on that compatibility
boundary is
a pre-upload gate.

