Live for Speed:

* Downloaded proprietary installer: LFS_S3_8C20_setup.exe
* Installer SHA-256:
  c06d3d9055f40e8e70994280a52b23f8c3c59b24ad726380547f0ed8899b9b76
* Vendor download page: https://www.lfs.net/downloads
* Vendor terms: https://www.lfs.net/agreement

The wrapper does not mirror, proxy, modify, or redistribute these artifacts.
The release-engineering worktree retained local operational C20 audit output
under `artifacts/`, which is intentionally untracked and omitted from release
source archives. It is not public source-package evidence; provide it directly
to a sponsor on request. The manifests and executable verification logic used
at runtime are included in the source package.

Git and upload binding gate
---------------------------

The orig tarball above is byte-identical to the published `v0.3.2` asset and
maps to upstream Git commit `4355f776cc5c0f6d2bd160986945a687666d5886`.
The current Debian directory is a review draft, not an upload identity. Before
signing or uploading, move the packaging to the sponsor-approved public VCS,
replace the draft Vcs fields, commit the complete Debian delta, and rebuild the
`.dsc` from a clean checkout of that exact commit. Record the commit, `.dsc`,
orig, Debian tarball, and buildinfo digests together. A clean build alone is
not evidence of correspondence to a public Git revision.

Build and test
--------------

Use a clean unstable chroot and build as an unprivileged user, for example:

  sbuild --dist=unstable --arch=amd64 --source --no-clean-source

The upstream build tests include static public-key/signature fixtures for real
`gpgv` acceptance, wrong-signer and bad-signature rejection, and a missing-
`VALIDSIG` parser case. Locally generated archive fixtures cover absolute and
parent paths, duplicate normalized members, escaping links, hardlinks, special
types, replacement ordering, safe links, and non-empty extraction destinations.
No private test key is included.

Run the installed-package tests with autopkgtest. They use only local package
content and do not contact Live for Speed, Arch Linux, GitHub, or WineHQ.
Before an initial upload, replace UNRELEASED in debian/changelog, add the ITP
bug as `Closes: #nnnnnn`, and use the approved maintainer and Salsa fields.
